  "title": "81: al-Takweer التكوير",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nاِذَا الشَّمْسُ كُوِّرَتْۙ‏(1)\nEZASH SHAMSO KUWWERAT.\nWhen the sun is wound up,\nوَاِذَا النُّجُوْمُ انْكَدَرَتْۙ‏(2)\nWA EZAN NOJOOMUN KADARAT.\nwhen the stars scatter,\nوَاِذَا الْجِبَالُ سُيِّرَتْۙ‏(3)\nWA EZAL JEBAALO SUYYERAT.\nwhen the mountains are set moving,\nوَاِذَا الْعِشَارُ عُطِّلَتْۙ‏(4)\nWA EZAL E’SHAARO U’TTELAT.\nwhen the pregnant camels are neglected,\nوَاِذَا الْوُحُوْشُ حُشِرَتْۙ‏(5)\nWA EZAL WOHOOSO HOSHERAT.\nwhen the wild beasts are mustered,\nوَاِذَا الْبِحَارُ سُجِّرَتْۙ‏(6)\nWA EZAL BEHAARO SUJJERAT.\nwhen the seas are set afire,\nوَاِذَا النُّفُوْسُ زُوِّجَتْۙ‏(7)\nWA EZAN NOFOOSO ZUWWEJAT.\nwhen the souls are assorted,\nوَاِذَا الْمَوْءٗدَةُ سُئِلَتْۙ‏(8)\nWA EZAL MAWOODATO SO-ELAT.\nwhen the girl buried-alive will be asked\nبِاَىِّ ذَنْۢبٍ قُتِلَتْ‌ۚ‏(9)\nBE-AYYE ZAMBIN QOTELAT.\nfor what sin she was killed.\nوَاِذَا الصُّحُفُ نُشِرَتْۙ‏(10)\nWA EZAS SOHOFO NOSHERAT.\nWhen the records [of deeds] are unfolded,\nوَاِذَا السَّمَآءُ كُشِطَتْۙ‏(11)\nWA EZAS SAMAAA-O KOSHETAT.\nwhen the sky is stripped off,\nوَاِذَا الْجَحِيْمُ سُعِّرَتْۙ‏(12)\nWA EZAL JAHEEMO SO’-E’RAT.\nwhen hell is set ablaze,\nوَاِذَا الْجَنَّةُ اُزْلِفَتْۙ‏(13)\nWA EZAL JANNATO UZLEFAT.\nwhen paradise is brought near,\nعَلِمَتْ نَفْسٌ مَّاۤ اَحْضَرَتْؕ‏(14)\nA’LEMAT NAFSUM MAA AHZARAT.\nthen a soul shall know what it has readied [for itself].\nفَلَاۤ اُقْسِمُ بِالْخُنَّسِۙ‏(15)\nFALAA UQSEMO BIL-KHUNNASIL\nSo I swear by the stars that return,\nالْجَوَارِ الْكُنَّسِۙ‏(16)\nJAWAARIL KUNNASE.\nthe comets,\nوَالَّيْلِ اِذَا عَسْعَسَۙ‏(17)\nWAL LAYLE EZAA A’S-A’SA.\nby the night as it approaches,\nوَالصُّبْحِ اِذَا تَنَفَّسَۙ‏(18)\nWAS SUBHE EZAA TANAFFASA.\nby the dawn as it breathes:\nاِنَّهٗ لَقَوْلُ رَسُوْلٍ كَرِيْمٍۙ‏(19)\nINNAHU LA-QAWLO RASOOLIN KAREEMIN.\nit is indeed the speech of a noble apostle,\nذِىْ قُوَّةٍ عِنْدَ ذِى الْعَرْشِ مَكِيْنٍۙ‏(20)\nZEE QUWWATIN I’NDA ZIL A’RSHIL MAKEENIM.\npowerful and eminent with the Lord of the Throne,\nمُّطَاعٍ ثَمَّ اَمِيْنٍؕ‏(21)\nMOTAA-I’N SAMMA AMEEN.\none who is obeyed and is trustworthy as well.\nوَ مَا صَاحِبُكُمْ بِمَجْنُوْنٍ‌ۚ‏(22)\nWA MAA SAAHEBOKUM BEMAJNOON.\nYour companion is not crazy:\nوَلَقَدْ رَاٰهُ بِالْاُفُقِ الْمُبِيْنِ‌ۚ‏(23)\nWA LAQAD RA-AAHO BIL-OFOQIL MOBEEN.\ncertainly he saw him on the manifest horizon,\nوَمَا هُوَ عَلَى الْغَيْبِ بِضَنِيْنٍ‌ۚ‏(24)\nWA MAA HOWA A’LAL GHAYBE BE-ZANEEN.\nand he is not miserly concerning the Unseen.\nوَمَا هُوَ بِقَوْلِ شَيْطٰنٍ رَّجِيْمٍۙ‏(25)\nWA MAA HOWA BE-QAWLE SHAYTAANIR RAJEEMIN.\nAnd it is not the speech of an outcast Satan.\nفَاَيْنَ تَذْهَبُوْنَؕ‏(26)\nFA-AYNA TAZHABOON.\nSo where are you going?\nاِنْ هُوَ اِلَّا ذِكْرٌ لِّلْعٰلَمِيْنَۙ‏(27)\nIN HOWA ILLAA ZIKRUL LIL-A’ALAMEENA.\nIt is just a reminder for all the nations,\nلِمَنْ شَآءَ مِنْكُمْ اَنْ يَّسْتَقِيْمَؕ‏(28)\nLEMAN SHAAA-A MINKUM AN-Y YASTAQEEM.\nfor those of you who wish to walk straight;\nوَمَا تَشَآءُوْنَ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ يَّشَآءَ اللّٰهُ رَبُّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(29)\nWA MAA TASHAAA-OONA ILLAA AN-Y YASHAAA-AL LAAHO RABBUL A’ALAMEEN.\nbut you will not wish unless it is wished by Allah, the Lord of all the worlds.",
  "merits": "Surah al-Takweer (The Covering Up)\nThis ‘Makki’ Surah has 29 verses. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said that the person who recites this Surah will be happy on the day when the book of deeds of people will be opened. Whoever wishes that Allah (s.w.t.) should show him His Mercy on the Day of Judgement should recite this Surah.\nRecitation of this Surah is especially good for the eyes. It improves vision and removes any ailments of the eyes."
